    "narrative": "For the Austin Waves on August 23, 2026, the lineup is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.47), both of whom benefit from highly favorable matchups against Nick Martinez and Carlos Rod\u00f3n, respectively. **Gunnar Henderson** remains our strongest play of the day; his 17% boost from the opposing SP skill and a 14% platoon edge against a right-hander solidify his status as an elite start. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) is a high-upside play against Bailey Ober, where his 19% SP skill boost and an additional 2% credit for a slow pitcher delivery make him a prime candidate to steal a base\u2014a critical factor given our prioritization of speed. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** also projects as a strong start (71.65) by leveraging a 14% dynamic platoon advantage in the three-hole against Javy Soriano.\n\nThe most difficult decision for today's roster construction centered on the UTIL slot, where **Tommy White** (54.84) narrowly edged out **Miguel Vargas** (44.77). While **Miguel Vargas** boasts a solid 0.387 xwOBA, his efficiency score was dragged down by the matchup against McLean and a negative impact from the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time. Ultimately, **Tommy White**\u2019s massive 19% SP skill adjustment against Cristian Javier outweighed the marginal gains offered by **Miguel Vargas**. We are also keeping a close watch on the volatility at the bottom of the order, specifically with **Drake Baldwin** (57.14) and **Luis Lara** (43.58); both are reliant on assumed batting orders due to pending lineups. Should **Drake Baldwin** shift down from the leadoff spot, his 10% order bonus will vanish, potentially dragging his daily efficiency score below our preferred 60.0 threshold.",
